--- Groups the elements of a list by a key function.
---
--- @details
--- `group_by` takes `[key_fn, xs]` and returns an object mapping each
--- distinct `key_fn(x)` (stringified) to the list of elements that
--- produced it. Groups are keyed in sorted order. It is the
--- `comb`-surface spelling of `combinators.group_by`.
---
--- @example
--- `[x ~> x % 2, [1, 2, 3, 4]] >>> comb.group_by`
--- -- => { "0": [2, 4], "1": [1, 3] }
---
export group_by :: [key_fn, xs] ~> combinators.group_by(key_fn, xs)
